  runs/**/*.pt
      Model checkpoints. Each stores the central-complex adjacency matrix (core.M) and cell-type
      index sets built from FlyWire snapshot 783 connections and cell-type annotations, synaptic
      weights trained on that adjacency, and, for the anatomical heading decoder, EPG
      ellipsoid-body angles measured on FlyWire neuron skeletons.

  docs/media/fly_brain_3d.gif
      Rendered from FlyWire snapshot 783 neuron skeletons and cell-type annotations.

Changes made to the source data: synapse counts summed per neuron pair across neuropils,
thresholded at 5 synapses, self-loops removed, and restricted to 457 central-complex neurons
(ER, EPG, PEN, PEG, Delta7, PFL3); skeletons downsampled for rendering.

FlyWire states that published versions of its data are available under CC BY-NC 4.0
(https://edit.flywire.ai/principles.html). Some FlyWire releases on Zenodo carry CC BY 4.0
(doi:10.5281/zenodo.10676866, doi:10.5281/zenodo.10877326); the stricter terms are used here
because the connectivity and annotation tables were downloaded from FlyWire Codex.

